                    {
                        "form_id": "dfa33231-6a74-43a0-9f7d-f1334502114b",
                        "entry_id": "1c6a7877-2063-3e2a-a621-2bcc62b967fa",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "shapeshifted"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "19644272-b042-3f76-9d71-c305ab6f405f",
                        "entry_id": "1c6a7877-2063-3e2a-a621-2bcc62b967fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To change one's shape or form (into another) through often magical means, normally applied only to living beings."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8994b4c-a6ea-4599-978f-519c405818e3",
                                "sense_id": "19644272-b042-3f76-9d71-c305ab6f405f",
                                "text": "I can't shapeshift Zane, I only look like this I always have."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e03cbb1b-2ece-4b0a-acdb-eef6139a8efc",
                                "sense_id": "19644272-b042-3f76-9d71-c305ab6f405f",
                                "text": "But to embed oneself in an irregular and unpredictable food supply as mycelium does, one must be able to shapeshift."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86c0557d-3af8-4d80-a461-c67f5adf4216",
                                "sense_id": "19644272-b042-3f76-9d71-c305ab6f405f",
                                "text": "For it was by shape-shifting and magic art, as poets tell, that Paris first beguiled Fair Helen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eda4a87e-152f-4218-b3c4-1b796abb5d93",
                                "sense_id": "19644272-b042-3f76-9d71-c305ab6f405f",
                                "text": "Journey in exactly the same way as you did to shapeshift into your power animal except, this time, set your intention to shapeshift into a named ancestor."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "85acba3f-a9ae-32af-a953-6fdf6c548b8f",
                        "entry_id": "1c6a7877-2063-3e2a-a621-2bcc62b967fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To undergo a noticeable change (in character for example), to metamorphosize."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4dd43dab-481b-4a5d-af00-698e509ea7d4",
                                "sense_id": "85acba3f-a9ae-32af-a953-6fdf6c548b8f",
                                "text": "While Chelsea Wolfe has often shapeshifted in terms of how she presents her music, one thing remains constant: her big mood."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
